IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc12-logic`

-- ccc12-part9-forgery.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part IX, "Forgery and Offences Resembling Forgery": sections 366 to 378.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc12-part9-theft.l4 and NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc12)").
-- Answers taken from another provision are INPUTS named for that provision (`s 2 <term>: ...`, `s 321 ...`, `s 25.1(1) ...`, `s 787(1) ...`); never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Forgery and Offences Resembling Forgery (ss 366 to 378)`

§§ `Section 366 -- forgery`

-- src:7049 | Forgery
-- src:7050 | 366 (1) Every one commits forgery who makes a false document, knowing it to be false, with intent
-- src:7051 | (a) that it should in any way be used or acted on as genuine, to the prejudice of any one whether within Canada or not; or
-- src:7052 | (b) that a person should be induced, by the belief that it is genuine, to do or to refrain from doing anything, whether within Canada or not.
@ref Criminal Code s 366(1) (src:7049-7052)
GIVEN `the document is a false document, by s 321 the document is a false document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person makes the false document, including by an act within subsection 366(2), by s 366(2) the act is making a false document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person knows it to be false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends that it should in any way be used or acted on as genuine, to the prejudice of any one whether within Canada or not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends that a person should be induced, by the belief that it is genuine, to do or to refrain from doing anything, whether within Canada or not` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(1) the person commits forgery` MEANS
    `ccc12 and` (`ccc12 and` `the document is a false document, by s 321 the document is a false document` `the person makes the false document, including by an act within subsection 366(2), by s 366(2) the act is making a false document`)
                (JUST (`the person knows it to be false` AND (`the person intends that it should in any way be used or acted on as genuine, to the prejudice of any one whether within Canada or not` OR `the person intends that a person should be induced, by the belief that it is genuine, to do or to refrain from doing anything, whether within Canada or not`)))
    -- JUST FALSE where it is not a false document, the person did not make it, did not know it to be false or had neither intent: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits forgery who makes a false document, knowing it to be false, with intent"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 321 "false document" or the s 366(2) "making" answer was not given

DECLARE `s 366(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 366(2)(a) altering a genuine document in any material part`
    `s 366(2)(b) making a material addition to a genuine document or adding to it a false date, attestation, seal or other thing that is material`
    `s 366(2)(c) making a material alteration in a genuine document by erasure, obliteration, removal or in any other way`
    `s 366(2) another act`

-- src:7053 | Making false document
-- src:7054 | (2) Making a false document includes
-- src:7055 | (a) altering a genuine document in any material part;
-- src:7056 | (b) making a material addition to a genuine document or adding to it a false date, attestation, seal or other thing that is material; or
-- src:7057 | (c) making a material alteration in a genuine document by erasure, obliteration, removal or in any other way.
@ref Criminal Code s 366(2) (src:7053-7057)
GIVEN act IS A `s 366(2) act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(2) the act is making a false document` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 366(2)(a) altering a genuine document in any material part` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 366(2)(b) making a material addition to a genuine document or adding to it a false date, attestation, seal or other thing that is material` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 366(2)(c) making a material alteration in a genuine document by erasure, obliteration, removal or in any other way` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 366(2) another act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Making a false document includes" lists three acts without closing the list

-- src:7058 | When forgery complete
-- src:7059 | (3) Forgery is complete as soon as a document is made with the knowledge and intent referred to in subsection (1), notwithstanding that the person who makes it does not intend that any particular person should use or act on it as genuine or be induced, by the belief that it is genuine, to do or refrain from doing anything.
@ref Criminal Code s 366(3) (src:7058-7059)
GIVEN `a document is made with the knowledge and intent referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(3) forgery is complete` MEANS
    IF `a document is made with the knowledge and intent referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- whether or not the person intends that any particular person should use or act on it as genuine or be induced by the belief that it is genuine
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Forgery is complete as soon as a document is made with the knowledge and intent referred to in subsection (1)" ("as soon as" counts as "where": fork F-WHEN)

-- src:7060 | Forgery complete though document incomplete
-- src:7061 | (4) Forgery is complete notwithstanding that the false document is incomplete or does not purport to be a document that is binding in law, if it is such as to indicate that it was intended to be acted on as genuine.
@ref Criminal Code s 366(4) (src:7060-7061)
GIVEN `the false document is incomplete or does not purport to be a document that is binding in law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is such as to indicate that it was intended to be acted on as genuine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(4) forgery is complete notwithstanding that the false document is incomplete or does not purport to be binding in law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the false document is incomplete or does not purport to be a document that is binding in law`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of a false document that is incomplete or does not purport to be binding in law
        IF `it is such as to indicate that it was intended to be acted on as genuine`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is such as to indicate that it was intended to be acted on as genuine"

-- src:7062 | Exception
-- src:7063 | (5) No person commits forgery by reason only that the person, in good faith, makes a false document at the request of a police force, the Canadian Forces or a department or agency of the federal government or of a provincial government.
@ref Criminal Code s 366(5) (src:7062-7063)
GIVEN `the person made the false document in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made it at the request of a police force, the Canadian Forces or a department or agency of the federal government or of a provincial government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(5) the person commits forgery by reason only of making a false document in good faith at the request of a police force, the Canadian Forces or a government department or agency` MEANS
    IF `the person made the false document in good faith` AND `the person made it at the request of a police force, the Canadian Forces or a department or agency of the federal government or of a provincial government`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person commits forgery by reason only that the person, in good faith, makes a false document at the request of a police force, the Canadian Forces or a department or agency of the federal government or of a provincial government"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that" the person made it in good faith at such a request; outside that limit the subsection says nothing

-- src:7064 | Punishment for forgery
-- src:7065 | 367 Every one who commits forgery
-- src:7066 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years; or
-- src:7067 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 367 (src:7064-7067)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 367 the punishment for forgery` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (a) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction

§§ `Sections 368 to 369 -- forged documents, instruments, public officers, seals`

-- src:7068 | Use, trafficking or possession of forged document
-- src:7069 | 368 (1) Everyone commits an offence who, knowing or believing that a document is forged,
-- src:7070 | (a) uses, deals with or acts on it as if it were genuine;
-- src:7071 | (b) causes or attempts to cause any person to use, deal with or act on it as if it were genuine;
-- src:7072 | (c) transfers, sells or offers to sell it or makes it available, to any person, knowing that or being reckless as to whether an offence will be committed under paragraph (a) or (b); or
-- src:7073 | (d) possesses it with intent to commit an offence under any of paragraphs (a) to (c).
@ref Criminal Code s 368(1) (src:7068-7073)
GIVEN `the person knows or believes that the document is forged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses, deals with or acts on it as if it were genuine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person causes or attempts to cause any person to use, deal with or act on it as if it were genuine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person transfers, sells or offers to sell it or makes it available, to any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that or is reckless as to whether an offence will be committed under paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses it with intent to commit an offence under any of paragraphs (a) to (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368(1) the person commits the offence of using, trafficking in or possessing a forged document` MEANS
    IF    `the person knows or believes that the document is forged`
      AND (   `the person uses, deals with or acts on it as if it were genuine`
           OR `the person causes or attempts to cause any person to use, deal with or act on it as if it were genuine`
           OR (`the person transfers, sells or offers to sell it or makes it available, to any person` AND `the person knows that or is reckless as to whether an offence will be committed under paragraph (a) or (b)`)
           OR `the person possesses it with intent to commit an offence under any of paragraphs (a) to (c)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who, knowing or believing that a document is forged"

-- src:7074 | Punishment
-- src:7075 | (1.1) Everyone who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:7076 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:7077 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 368(1.1) (src:7074-7077)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 368(1.1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (a) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction

-- src:7078 | Wherever forged
-- src:7079 | (2) For the purposes of proceedings under this section, the place where a document was forged is not material.
@ref Criminal Code s 368(2) (src:7078-7079)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under section 368` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is the place where the document was forged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368(2) the place where the document was forged is material` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings under section 368` AND `the matter is the place where the document was forged`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of proceedings under this section, the place where a document was forged is not material"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of the place where a document was forged, in proceedings under section 368

-- src:7080 | Forgery instruments
-- src:7081 | 368.1 Everyone is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years, or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction, who, without lawful authority or excuse, makes, repairs, buys, sells, exports from Canada, imports into Canada or possesses any instrument, device, apparatus, material or thing that they know has been used or know is adapted or intended for use by any person to commit forgery.
@ref Criminal Code s 368.1 (src:7080-7081)
GIVEN `the person acted without lawful authority or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes, repairs, buys, sells, exports from Canada, imports into Canada or possesses the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the thing has been used, or knows that it is adapted or intended for use, by any person to commit forgery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368.1 the person commits the offence of possessing a forgery instrument` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted without lawful authority or excuse`
      AND `the person makes, repairs, buys, sells, exports from Canada, imports into Canada or possesses the thing`
      AND `the person knows that the thing has been used, or knows that it is adapted or intended for use, by any person to commit forgery`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone is guilty of an indictable offence ... who, without lawful authority or excuse, makes, repairs, buys, sells, exports from Canada, imports into Canada or possesses any instrument, device, apparatus, material or thing that they know has been used or know is adapted or intended for use by any person to commit forgery"

@ref Criminal Code s 368.1 (src:7081-7081)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 368.1 the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`)
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- 368.2: "No public officer, as defined in subsection 25.1(1), is guilty of an offence under any of sections 366 to 368.1 if ... for the sole purpose of establishing or maintaining a covert identity ..."
-- The section numbers are tested as a range of decimals (366 to 368.1: 367, 368 and 368.1 are inside, 369 is not).
-- src:7082 | Public officers acting in the course of their duties or employment
-- src:7083 | 368.2 No public officer, as defined in subsection 25.1(1), is guilty of an offence under any of sections 366 to 368.1 if the acts alleged to constitute the offence were committed by the public officer for the sole purpose of establishing or maintaining a covert identity for use in the course of the public officer’s duties or employment.
@ref Criminal Code s 368.2 (src:7082-7083)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person is a public officer, as defined in subsection 25.1(1), by s 25.1(1) public officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the acts alleged to constitute the offence were committed by the public officer for the sole purpose of establishing or maintaining a covert identity for use in the course of the public officer's duties or employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 368.2 the public officer is guilty of an offence under any of sections 366 to 368.1` MEANS
    IF `the offence`'s `section` AT LEAST 366 AND `the offence`'s `section` AT MOST 368.1 AND `the acts alleged to constitute the offence were committed by the public officer for the sole purpose of establishing or maintaining a covert identity for use in the course of the public officer's duties or employment`
    THEN CONSIDER `the person is a public officer, as defined in subsection 25.1(1), by s 25.1(1) public officer`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No public officer, as defined in subsection 25.1(1), is guilty of an offence under any of sections 366 to 368.1 if the acts alleged to constitute the offence were committed by the public officer for the sole purpose of establishing or maintaining a covert identity for use in the course of the public officer’s duties or employment"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section speaks of a public officer as defined in subsection 25.1(1)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the s 25.1(1) "public officer" answer was not given
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section speaks of "sections 366 to 368.1" and of acts "for the sole purpose" of a covert identity; outside that limit it says nothing

-- src:7084 | Exchequer bill paper, public seals, etc.
-- src:7085 | 369 Everyone is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years who, without lawful authority or excuse,
-- src:7086 | (a) makes, uses or possesses
-- src:7087 | (i) any exchequer bill paper, revenue paper or paper that is used to make bank-notes, or
-- src:7088 | (ii) any paper that is intended to resemble paper mentioned in subparagraph (i); or
-- src:7089 | (b) makes, reproduces or uses a public seal of Canada or of a province, or the seal of a public body or authority in Canada or of a court of law.
@ref Criminal Code s 369 (src:7084-7089)
GIVEN `the person acted without lawful authority or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes, uses or possesses the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is exchequer bill paper, by s 321 the paper is exchequer bill paper` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is revenue paper, by s 321 the paper is revenue paper` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is paper that is used to make bank-notes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is paper that is intended to resemble paper mentioned in subparagraph (a)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes, reproduces or uses a public seal of Canada or of a province, or the seal of a public body or authority in Canada or of a court of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 369 the person commits the offence of dealing in exchequer bill paper, revenue paper or public seals` MEANS
    IF `the person acted without lawful authority or excuse`
    THEN `ccc12 or` (`ccc12 and` (JUST `the person makes, uses or possesses the thing`) `paper`) (JUST `the person makes, reproduces or uses a public seal of Canada or of a province, or the seal of a public body or authority in Canada or of a court of law`)
         -- JUST FALSE where neither paragraph holds: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone is guilty of an indictable offence ... who, without lawful authority or excuse, (a) makes, uses or possesses (i) any exchequer bill paper, revenue paper or paper that is used to make bank-notes"
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 321 "exchequer bill paper" or "revenue paper" answer was not given and nothing else settles it
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who, without lawful authority or excuse"
    WHERE
        `paper` MEANS
            `ccc12 or` (`ccc12 or` `the thing is exchequer bill paper, by s 321 the paper is exchequer bill paper` `the thing is revenue paper, by s 321 the paper is revenue paper`)
                       (JUST (`the thing is paper that is used to make bank-notes` OR `the thing is paper that is intended to resemble paper mentioned in subparagraph (a)(i)`))

@ref Criminal Code s 369 (src:7085-7085)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 369 the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`)

-- src:7090 | 370 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 42]
@ref Criminal Code s 370 (src:7090)
`s 370 as the text shows it` MEANS "370 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 42]"

-- src:7091 | 371 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 42]
