`s 371 as the text shows it` MEANS "371 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 42]"

§§ `Section 372 -- false information, indecent and harassing communications`

-- src:7092 | False information
-- src:7093 | 372 (1) Everyone commits an offence who, with intent to injure or alarm a person, conveys information that they know is false, or causes such information to be conveyed by letter or any means of telecommunication.
@ref Criminal Code s 372(1) (src:7092-7093)
GIVEN `the person acted with intent to injure or alarm a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person conveys information that they know is false, or causes such information to be conveyed by letter or any means of telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 372(1) the person commits the offence of conveying false information` MEANS
    IF `the person acted with intent to injure or alarm a person` AND `the person conveys information that they know is false, or causes such information to be conveyed by letter or any means of telecommunication`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who, with intent to injure or alarm a person, conveys information that they know is false, or causes such information to be conveyed by letter or any means of telecommunication"

-- src:7094 | Indecent communications
-- src:7095 | (2) Everyone commits an offence who, with intent to alarm or annoy a person, makes an indecent communication to that person or to any other person by a means of telecommunication.
@ref Criminal Code s 372(2) (src:7094-7095)
GIVEN `the person acted with intent to alarm or annoy a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes an indecent communication to that person or to any other person by a means of telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 372(2) the person commits the offence of making an indecent communication` MEANS
    IF `the person acted with intent to alarm or annoy a person` AND `the person makes an indecent communication to that person or to any other person by a means of telecommunication`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who, with intent to alarm or annoy a person, makes an indecent communication to that person or to any other person by a means of telecommunication"

-- src:7096 | Harassing communications
-- src:7097 | (3) Everyone commits an offence who, without lawful excuse and with intent to harass a person, repeatedly communicates, or causes repeated communications to be made, with them by a means of telecommunication.
@ref Criminal Code s 372(3) (src:7096-7097)
GIVEN `the person acted without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted with intent to harass a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person repeatedly communicates, or causes repeated communications to be made, with them by a means of telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 372(3) the person commits the offence of making harassing communications` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted without lawful excuse`
      AND `the person acted with intent to harass a person`
      AND `the person repeatedly communicates, or causes repeated communications to be made, with them by a means of telecommunication`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone commits an offence who, without lawful excuse and with intent to harass a person, repeatedly communicates, or causes repeated communications to be made, with them by a means of telecommunication"

-- src:7098 | Punishment
-- src:7099 | (4) Everyone who commits an offence under this section is
-- src:7100 | (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:7101 | (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 372(4) (src:7098-7101)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 372(4) the punishment for an offence under section 372` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`)   -- (a) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than two years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction

-- src:7102 | 373 [Repealed, R.S., 1985, c. 27 (1st Supp.), s. 53]
@ref Criminal Code s 373 (src:7102)
`s 373 as the text shows it` MEANS "373 [Repealed, R.S., 1985, c. 27 (1st Supp.), s. 53]"

§§ `Sections 374 to 378 -- documents, stamps, marks, registers`

-- src:7103 | Drawing document without authority, etc.
-- src:7104 | 374 Every one who
-- src:7105 | (a) with intent to defraud and without lawful authority makes, executes, draws, signs, accepts or endorses a document in the name or on the account of another person by procuration or otherwise, or
-- src:7106 | (b) makes use of or utters a document knowing that it has been made, executed, signed, accepted or endorsed with intent to defraud and without lawful authority, in the name or on the account of another person, by procuration or otherwise,
-- src:7107 | is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 374 (src:7103-7107)
GIVEN `the thing is a document, by s 321 the thing is a document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `with intent to defraud and without lawful authority, the person makes, executes, draws, signs, accepts or endorses it in the name or on the account of another person by procuration or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes use of or utters it knowing that it has been made, executed, signed, accepted or endorsed with intent to defraud and without lawful authority, in the name or on the account of another person, by procuration or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 374 the person commits the offence of drawing or using a document without authority` MEANS
    `ccc12 and` `the thing is a document, by s 321 the thing is a document`
                (JUST (   `with intent to defraud and without lawful authority, the person makes, executes, draws, signs, accepts or endorses it in the name or on the account of another person by procuration or otherwise`
                       OR `the person makes use of or utters it knowing that it has been made, executed, signed, accepted or endorsed with intent to defraud and without lawful authority, in the name or on the account of another person, by procuration or otherwise`))
    -- JUST FALSE where neither paragraph holds or it is not a document: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who (a) with intent to defraud and without lawful authority makes, executes, draws, signs, accepts or endorses a document in the name or on the account of another person by procuration or otherwise"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 321 "document" answer was not given

@ref Criminal Code s 374 (src:7107-7107)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 374 the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`)

-- src:7108 | Obtaining, etc., by instrument based on forged document
-- src:7109 | 375 Every one who demands, receives or obtains anything, or causes or procures anything to be delivered or paid to any person under, on or by virtue of any instrument issued under the authority of law, knowing that it is based on a forged document, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 375 (src:7108-7109)
GIVEN `the person demands, receives or obtains anything, or causes or procures anything to be delivered or paid to any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so under, on or by virtue of an instrument issued under the authority of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the instrument is based on a forged document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 375 the person commits the offence of obtaining a thing by an instrument based on a forged document` MEANS
    IF    `the person demands, receives or obtains anything, or causes or procures anything to be delivered or paid to any person`
      AND `the person does so under, on or by virtue of an instrument issued under the authority of law`
      AND `the person knows that the instrument is based on a forged document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who demands, receives or obtains anything, or causes or procures anything to be delivered or paid to any person under, on or by virtue of any instrument issued under the authority of law, knowing that it is based on a forged document"

@ref Criminal Code s 375 (src:7109-7109)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 375 the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`)

-- src:7124 | Definitions
-- src:7125 | (3) In this section,
-- src:7126 | mark means a mark, brand, seal, wrapper or design used by or on behalf of
-- src:7127 | (a) the government of Canada or a province,
-- src:7128 | (b) the government of a state other than Canada, or
-- src:7129 | (c) any department, board, commission or agent established by a government mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) in connection with the service or business of that government; (marque)
@ref Criminal Code s 376(3) mark (src:7124-7129)
DECLARE `s 376(3) mark user` IS ONE OF
    `s 376(3)(a) used by or on behalf of the government of Canada or a province`
    `s 376(3)(b) used by or on behalf of the government of a state other than Canada`
    `s 376(3)(c) used by or on behalf of a department, board, commission or agent established by a government mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) in connection with the service or business of that government`
    `s 376(3) used by no one of those`

@ref Criminal Code s 376(3) mark (src:7126-7129)
GIVEN `it is a mark, brand, seal, wrapper or design` IS A BOOLEAN
      user IS A `s 376(3) mark user`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376(3) the thing is a mark` MEANS
    IF `it is a mark, brand, seal, wrapper or design`
    THEN CONSIDER user
         WHEN `s 376(3)(a) used by or on behalf of the government of Canada or a province` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 376(3)(b) used by or on behalf of the government of a state other than Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 376(3)(c) used by or on behalf of a department, board, commission or agent established by a government mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) in connection with the service or business of that government` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 376(3) used by no one of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "mark means a mark, brand, seal, wrapper or design used by or on behalf of"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "mark means a mark, brand, seal, wrapper or design"

-- src:7130 | stamp means an impressed or adhesive stamp used for the purpose of revenue by the government of Canada or a province or by the government of a state other than Canada. (timbre)
@ref Criminal Code s 376(3) stamp (src:7130)
GIVEN `it is an impressed or adhesive stamp` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used for the purpose of revenue by the government of Canada or a province or by the government of a state other than Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376(3) the thing is a stamp` MEANS
    IF `it is an impressed or adhesive stamp` AND `it is used for the purpose of revenue by the government of Canada or a province or by the government of a state other than Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "stamp means an impressed or adhesive stamp used for the purpose of revenue by the government of Canada or a province or by the government of a state other than Canada"

-- src:7110 | Counterfeiting stamp, etc.
-- src:7111 | 376 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years who
-- src:7112 | (a) fraudulently uses, mutilates, affixes, removes or counterfeits a stamp or part thereof,
-- src:7113 | (b) knowingly and without lawful excuse has in their possession
-- src:7114 | (i) a counterfeit stamp or a stamp that has been fraudulently mutilated, or
-- src:7115 | (ii) anything bearing a stamp of which a part has been fraudulently erased, removed or concealed, or
-- src:7116 | (c) without lawful excuse makes or knowingly has in their possession a die or instrument that is capable of making the impression of a stamp or part of a stamp.
@ref Criminal Code s 376(1) (src:7110-7116)
GIVEN `the thing is a stamp, by s 376(3) the thing is a stamp` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently uses, mutilates, affixes, removes or counterfeits a stamp or part thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly and without lawful excuse has in their possession a counterfeit stamp or a stamp that has been fraudulently mutilated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly and without lawful excuse has in their possession anything bearing a stamp of which a part has been fraudulently erased, removed or concealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person without lawful excuse makes or knowingly has in their possession a die or instrument that is capable of making the impression of a stamp or part of a stamp` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376(1) the person commits the offence of counterfeiting a stamp` MEANS
    `ccc12 and` `the thing is a stamp, by s 376(3) the thing is a stamp`
                (JUST (    `the person fraudulently uses, mutilates, affixes, removes or counterfeits a stamp or part thereof`
                        OR `the person knowingly and without lawful excuse has in their possession a counterfeit stamp or a stamp that has been fraudulently mutilated`
                        OR `the person knowingly and without lawful excuse has in their possession anything bearing a stamp of which a part has been fraudulently erased, removed or concealed`
                        OR `the person without lawful excuse makes or knowingly has in their possession a die or instrument that is capable of making the impression of a stamp or part of a stamp`))
    -- JUST FALSE where no paragraph holds or it is not a stamp: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years who (a) fraudulently uses, mutilates, affixes, removes or counterfeits a stamp or part thereof"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 376(3) "stamp" answer was not given

@ref Criminal Code s 376(1) (src:7111-7111)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 376(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`)

-- src:7117 | Counterfeiting mark
-- src:7118 | (2) Every one who, without lawful authority,
-- src:7119 | (a) makes a mark,
-- src:7120 | (b) sells, or exposes for sale, or has in his possession a counterfeit mark,
-- src:7121 | (c) affixes a mark to anything that is required by law to be marked, branded, sealed or wrapped other than the thing to which the mark was originally affixed or was intended to be affixed, or
-- src:7122 | (d) affixes a counterfeit mark to anything that is required by law to be marked, branded, sealed or wrapped,
-- src:7123 | is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 376(2) (src:7117-7123)
GIVEN `the person acted without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a mark, by s 376(3) the thing is a mark` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person makes a mark` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person sells, or exposes for sale, or has in their possession a counterfeit mark` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person affixes a mark to anything that is required by law to be marked, branded, sealed or wrapped other than the thing to which the mark was originally affixed or was intended to be affixed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person affixes a counterfeit mark to anything that is required by law to be marked, branded, sealed or wrapped` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376(2) the person commits the offence of counterfeiting a mark` MEANS
    IF `the person acted without lawful authority`
    THEN `ccc12 and` `the thing is a mark, by s 376(3) the thing is a mark`
                     (JUST (    `the person makes a mark`
                             OR `the person sells, or exposes for sale, or has in their possession a counterfeit mark`
                             OR `the person affixes a mark to anything that is required by law to be marked, branded, sealed or wrapped other than the thing to which the mark was originally affixed or was intended to be affixed`
                             OR `the person affixes a counterfeit mark to anything that is required by law to be marked, branded, sealed or wrapped`))
         -- JUST FALSE where no paragraph holds or it is not a mark; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 376(3) "mark" answer was not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who, without lawful authority"

@ref Criminal Code s 376(2) (src:7123-7123)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 376(2) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`)

-- src:7137 | Definition of election document
-- src:7138 | (2) In this section, election document means any document or writing issued under the authority of an Act of Parliament or the legislature of a province with respect to an election held pursuant to the authority of that Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 377(2) (src:7137-7138)
GIVEN `it is a document or writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is issued under the authority of an Act of Parliament or the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is with respect to an election held pursuant to the authority of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(2) the document is an election document` MEANS
    IF `it is a document or writing` AND `it is issued under the authority of an Act of Parliament or the legislature of a province` AND `it is with respect to an election held pursuant to the authority of that Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "election document means any document or writing issued under the authority of an Act of Parliament or the legislature of a province with respect to an election held pursuant to the authority of that Act"

-- src:7131 | Damaging documents
-- src:7132 | 377 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who unlawfully
-- src:7133 | (a) destroys, defaces or injures a register, or any part of a register, of births, baptisms, marriages, deaths or burials that is required or authorized by law to be kept in Canada, or a copy or any part of a copy of such a register that is required by law to be transmitted to a registrar or other officer,
-- src:7134 | (b) inserts or causes to be inserted in a register or copy referred to in paragraph (a) an entry, that he knows is false, of any matter relating to a birth, baptism, marriage, death or burial, or erases any material part from that register or copy,
-- src:7135 | (c) destroys, damages or obliterates an election document or causes an election document to be destroyed, damaged or obliterated, or
-- src:7136 | (d) makes or causes to be made an erasure, alteration or interlineation in or on an election document.
@ref Criminal Code s 377(1) (src:7131-7136)
GIVEN `the person acted unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person destroys, defaces or injures a register, or any part of a register, of births, baptisms, marriages, deaths or burials that is required or authorized by law to be kept in Canada, or a copy or any part of a copy of such a register that is required by law to be transmitted to a registrar or other officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person inserts or causes to be inserted in a register or copy referred to in paragraph (a) an entry, that they know is false, of any matter relating to a birth, baptism, marriage, death or burial, or erases any material part from that register or copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is an election document, by s 377(2) the document is an election document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person destroys, damages or obliterates an election document or causes an election document to be destroyed, damaged or obliterated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes or causes to be made an erasure, alteration or interlineation in or on an election document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(1) the person commits the offence of damaging documents` MEANS
    IF `the person acted unlawfully`
    THEN `ccc12 or` (JUST (`the person destroys, defaces or injures a register, or any part of a register, of births, baptisms, marriages, deaths or burials that is required or authorized by law to be kept in Canada, or a copy or any part of a copy of such a register that is required by law to be transmitted to a registrar or other officer` OR `the person inserts or causes to be inserted in a register or copy referred to in paragraph (a) an entry, that they know is false, of any matter relating to a birth, baptism, marriage, death or burial, or erases any material part from that register or copy`))
                    (`ccc12 and` `the thing is an election document, by s 377(2) the document is an election document` (JUST (`the person destroys, damages or obliterates an election document or causes an election document to be destroyed, damaged or obliterated` OR `the person makes or causes to be made an erasure, alteration or interlineation in or on an election document`)))
         -- JUST FALSE where no paragraph holds or it is not an election document; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 377(2) "election document" answer was not given and paragraphs (a) and (b) do not hold
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence ... who unlawfully"

@ref Criminal Code s 377(1) (src:7132-7132)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 377(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`)
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:7139 | Offences in relation to registers
-- src:7140 | 378 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:7141 | (a) being authorized or required by law to make or issue a certified copy of, extract from or certificate in respect of a register, record or document, knowingly makes or issues a false certified copy, extract or certificate,
-- src:7142 | (b) not being authorized or required by law to make or issue a certified copy of, extract from or certificate in respect of a register, record or document, fraudulently makes or issues a copy, extract or certificate that purports to be certified as authorized or required by law, or
-- src:7143 | (c) being authorized or required by law to make a certificate or declaration concerning any particular required for the purpose of making entries in a register, record or document, knowingly and falsely makes the certificate or declaration.
@ref Criminal Code s 378 (src:7139-7143)
GIVEN `the person is authorized or required by law to make or issue a certified copy of, extract from or certificate in respect of a register, record or document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly makes or issues a false certified copy, extract or certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently makes or issues a copy, extract or certificate that purports to be certified as authorized or required by law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorized or required by law to make a certificate or declaration concerning any particular required for the purpose of making entries in a register, record or document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly and falsely makes the certificate or declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378 the person commits an offence in relation to registers` MEANS
    IF    (`the person is authorized or required by law to make or issue a certified copy of, extract from or certificate in respect of a register, record or document` AND `the person knowingly makes or issues a false certified copy, extract or certificate`)
       OR ((NOT `the person is authorized or required by law to make or issue a certified copy of, extract from or certificate in respect of a register, record or document`) AND `the person fraudulently makes or issues a copy, extract or certificate that purports to be certified as authorized or required by law`)
       OR (`the person is authorized or required by law to make a certificate or declaration concerning any particular required for the purpose of making entries in a register, record or document` AND `the person knowingly and falsely makes the certificate or declaration`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person is guilty of an indictable offence ... who (a) being authorized or required by law to make or issue a certified copy of, extract from or certificate in respect of a register, record or document, knowingly makes or issues a false certified copy, extract or certificate"

@ref Criminal Code s 378 (src:7140-7140)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 378 the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`)
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
